/* M3_script template.

   Run:  monarch screen-script this.fountain --length short --board-out board.json

   The maths line decides everything: at 60s that is 18 beats x 7 words exact.
   One spoken beat = one clip = one scene board row.

   Law:
   - never pad to reach the count; write the words or pick a longer --length
   - duration is words / speaking_wps — never invent clip timing by hand
   - every scene needs a visual and a retention job (the gate fails closed)
   - dialogue and action are separated by blank lines (Fountain law)
*/


EXT. <PLACE> - <TIME> #1#

VOICEOVER (V.O.)
::<visual: what the stickman is doing>:: <exactly n words that force the watch>


EXT. <PLACE> - CONTINUOUS #2#

VOICEOVER (V.O.)
::<visual: the next picture, match-cut friendly>:: <exactly n words of new information>


/* ... one block per scene — the count comes from:
   monarch maths --seconds 60  */


EXT. <PLACE> - DAWN #18#

VOICEOVER (V.O.)
::<visual: the callback that pays the open loop>:: <exactly n words of payoff>
